# W44-PHASE3-B5b — iter-0 GPU/CPU butteraugli divergence detector

**Date**: 2026-05-24
**Status**: [RULED OUT — implementation shipped, design fundamentally unsound]
**Bench wall**: ~12 minutes (38 cells × 3 modes × 3 time-iters; mode B and C
both run buttloop at GPU speed so total is roughly 2-3× the CPU-only bench)

## What was tested

The W44-PHASE3-B5 honest-stop memo
(`memory/w44_phase3_b5_gpu_wider_sweep_2026-05-23.md`) documented 3 paths
to unblock the `gpu-butteraugli` default-on flip. Path #2 was the
**per-iter divergence detector + CPU fallback**:

> On every buttloop iteration when running gpu-butteraugli, compute GPU
> butteraugli score AND a cheap CPU sanity check; if they diverge by
> more than a threshold, fall back to CPU for the remaining iterations
> of THIS cell. This lets us default-flip GPU on with safety: GPU wins
> on the 36/38 cells, CPU rescues the 2 divergent cells.

After analysing the buttloop's per-iter compare site, the cheapest path
turned out to be **iter-0 only** (not per-iter): run BOTH GPU and CPU
butteraugli compute on iter 0, compare scores, fall back to CPU shadow
for the rest of the cell if `|gpu - cpu| / max(|gpu|, |cpu|) > 0.5%`.
Per-iter shadow would have ≥4× wall cost (defeats the GPU speedup).

## Implementation

`jxl-encoder/src/vardct/butteraugli_backend.rs`:
- `GpuButteraugliBackend` extended with:
  - `cpu_shadow: Option<Box<CpuButteraugliBackend>>` — lazy-allocated
    when env var `JXL_W44_PHASE3_B5B_DETECTOR=1` is set
  - `compare_call_count: u32`, `forced_to_cpu: bool`,
    `last_divergence_pct: Option<f64>` — per-cell state
- `GPU_SCORE_DIVERGENCE_PCT = 0.005` — the 0.5% threshold W44-phase3-B1
  documented (re-used; previously was inert)
- `W44_PHASE3_B5B_ENV = "JXL_W44_PHASE3_B5B_DETECTOR"` — env gate
- `set_reference` now also caches reference into shadow CPU (if Some);
  resets per-cell detector state
- `compare_with_reference` on iter-0: runs GPU; runs CPU shadow; computes
  `divergence_pct`; if `> threshold` flips `forced_to_cpu` and returns
  the CPU result. On iter ≥1 routes through shadow only if forced,
  else GPU.
- New `ButteraugliBackend::divergence_status() -> Option<(f64, bool)>`
  trait method; CPU impl returns None (default), GPU impl returns
  `Some((divergence_pct, forced_to_cpu))` after iter 0.
- Process-global counter module `b5b_counters` (re-exposed via
  `crate::vardct::__b5b_counters` for the bench harness) tracks
  `run_count + fallback_count + divergence_pct_sum + divergence_pct_max`
  across all backend instances; reset between cells.

`construct_backend` extended to clone `cpu_params` into
`GpuButteraugliBackend::try_new` when `JXL_W44_PHASE3_B5B_DETECTOR=1`
is set in the environment at the time of construction. Default
behaviour (env unset) → shadow=None → byte-identical to pre-B5b.

`examples/w44_phase3_b5b_divergence_detector_ab.rs` — 38-cell × 3-mode
A/B harness (CPU baseline; GPU without detector; GPU with detector).
Per-cell `b5b_counters::reset()` + post-encode `snapshot()` to capture
detector observations.

